Subject: 6.6.y: btusb fails to build with CONFIG_WERROR=y and BT_MTK off

Hello,

since v6.6.142, drivers/bluetooth/btusb.o fails to build on 6.6.y
when CONFIG_BT_MTK is off and CONFIG_WERROR=y (x86_64 defconfig,
BT=m, BT_HCIBTUSB=m; also with W=1):

  drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.h:232:13: error: 'btmtk_fw_get_filename'
    defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]
  drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.h:221:12: error: 'btmtk_register_coredump'
    defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]
  drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.h:211:12: error: 'btmtk_setup_firmware'
    defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]
  drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.h:205:12: error: 'btmtk_setup_firmware_79xx'
    defined but not used [-Werror=unused-function]

v6.6.141 builds; v6.6.142 does not, and neither does v6.6.161. It
came with b748250d778e ("Bluetooth: btmtk: add the function to get the
fw name"), the 6.6.y backport of 00f993fdec06, which adds a
non-inline static stub for the !CONFIG_BT_MTK case
(btmtk_fw_get_filename); the other three errors appear from v6.6.145
on. Mainline fixed the
stubs with 23e88450bb04 ("Bluetooth: btmtk: Mark all stub functions as
inline"), which is not in 6.6.y and does not cherry-pick cleanly onto
v6.6.161 (conflict in drivers/bluetooth/btmtk.h).

Would you take an adapted backport of 23e88450bb04 for 6.6.y? I can
send one.

Thank you,
Iaroslav Voitovych
